    <summary>A Deza graph G with parameters (n,k,b,a) is a k-regular graph with n vertices such that any two distinct vertices have b or a common neighbours, where b &gt;= a. The children G_A and G_B of a Deza graph G are defined on the vertex set of G such that every two distinct vertices are adjacent in G_A or G_B if and only if they have a or b common neighbours, respectively. In this paper we present a general approach to dual Seidel switching and investigate Deza graphs whose children are strongly regular graphs.</summary>
